    name: "Screenplay scene in a hospital cafeteria",
    expect: "script",
    text: `NIGHT SHIFT
Written by Dana Okonkwo
Draft 2 – Intro to Screenwriting

FADE IN:

INT. HOSPITAL CAFETERIA - NIGHT

Fluorescent lights buzz over rows of empty tables. A vending machine glows in the corner.

ROSALIND (50s), a nurse in faded blue scrubs with reading glasses on a beaded chain, sits alone doing a crossword. A tray of untouched green gelatin sits beside her.

THEO (24), a new resident, his badge still stiff and shiny, hovers nearby with a paper cup of coffee.

THEO
Is it okay if I sit here?

ROSALIND
(without looking up)
The chairs aren't assigned.

He sits. Sips. Winces.

THEO
This coffee is...

ROSALIND
Free. That's the nicest thing anyone says about it.

A beat. Theo stares at the table. His hands are shaking slightly.

ROSALIND (CONT'D)
First one?

THEO
First what?

ROSALIND
First patient you lost.

Theo looks up, startled.

THEO
How did you...

ROSALIND
You've been holding that coffee for ten minutes and you haven't noticed it's cold.

Theo sets the cup down. He laughs, but it cracks in the middle.

THEO
Mr. Kowalczyk. Room 412. He asked me to bring him a newspaper in the morning. I said sure.

Rosalind finally puts down her pen.

ROSALIND
Six letters. "Something you keep even when you can't." Starts with P.

THEO
(confused)
I don't...

ROSALIND
Promise.

She slides the newspaper from under her crossword across the table to him.

ROSALIND (CONT'D)
Room 412 is still made up till six. Go put it on the nightstand. Then come back and help me with seventeen across.

Theo stares at the newspaper. Then he picks it up and stands.

THEO
What's seventeen across?

ROSALIND
(back to her puzzle)
I'll tell you when you get back.

He goes. Rosalind watches him leave, then pushes the gelatin a little farther away.

FADE OUT.`,
