    text: `The Lost and Found
A One-Act Play by Grace Oyelowo
Drama 2 – Original Scene Assignment

CHARACTERS
MRS. PELL, a school custodian in her sixties
JONAH, a seventh grader
AVA, Jonah's older sister, a ninth grader

SETTING: A middle school hallway after dismissal. A large cardboard box marked LOST AND FOUND sits against a wall of lockers, overflowing with sweatshirts, water bottles and a single rain boot.

(Lights up. MRS. PELL pushes a mop bucket across the stage. JONAH is on his knees, digging through the box.)

MRS. PELL: That's three days in a row you've been in that box.
JONAH: (not looking up) I lost something.
MRS. PELL: Everybody who goes in that box lost something. That's the whole idea of the box.
JONAH: It's a jacket. Green. It has a patch on the sleeve shaped like a fox.
MRS. PELL: (leaning on her mop) Hm. Haven't seen a fox.
(AVA enters, backpack over one shoulder, earbuds in. She stops when she sees JONAH.)
AVA: Mom's in the car. Come on.
JONAH: One more minute.
AVA: (pulling out an earbud) Jonah, it's not here. You checked yesterday.
JONAH: You don't know that.
AVA: (quieter) It was Dad's jacket. I know.
(A pause. MRS. PELL stops mopping.)
MRS. PELL: Your dad's?
JONAH: He wore it to every one of my games. I wore it on Monday and I left it somewhere and now it's just... gone.
(MRS. PELL sets down the mop, crosses to her cart, and pulls a folded green jacket from the bottom shelf.)
MRS. PELL: Found it in the gym Monday night. Patch was coming loose, so I took it home and sewed it back on. I was going to put it in the box tomorrow.
(JONAH takes the jacket. He runs his thumb over the fox patch. He can't speak.)
AVA: (softly) Thank you.
MRS. PELL: (picking up the mop again) Things don't stay lost around here if I can help it. Go on. Your mom's waiting.
(JONAH puts on the jacket. AVA puts an arm around his shoulders, and they exit. MRS. PELL looks at the box, then straightens a sweatshirt on top of the pile.)
(Lights fade.)
END OF PLAY`,
