    name: "Public comment at a city council meeting",
    expect: "speech",
    text: `Public Comment – City Council Meeting, Item 7 (Elm Street Crosswalk)

Good evening, Mayor Torres and members of the council. My name is Gabriel Ashford, and I live at the corner of Elm and Fourth, about fifty feet from the spot we're talking about tonight. I know I only have three minutes, so I'll get right to it.

I'm here to ask you to approve the flashing crosswalk on Elm Street.

Every school day, I watch about sixty kids cross Elm on their way to Garfield Elementary. There's no light and no crossing guard after 8:15. Cars come down that hill at forty, sometimes fifty miles an hour, and by the time they see a kid in the road, they're already halfway through the intersection.

Last October, a fourth grader named Luis was clipped by a pickup truck right in front of my house. He was lucky. He walked away with a broken wrist. I was the one who called 911, and I can tell you that I still hear the sound of those brakes.

Since then, my neighbors and I have collected two hundred and twelve signatures. We've counted traffic. We've talked to the principal. And your own staff report, on page four, says this crossing meets every standard for a flashing beacon.

I understand the budget is tight. But the cost of this crosswalk is about the same as one month of overtime for the street department. The cost of not doing it could be a child's life.

So I'm asking you, please, don't wait for the next accident. Vote yes on item seven.

Thank you for your time. I'm happy to answer any questions.`,
