    text: `Earth Science – Unit 3 Study Guide
Weathering, Erosion & Deposition
Test: Friday 11/14

● Weathering = breaking down rock where it is (does NOT move it)
    ○ Mechanical (physical): rock breaks into smaller pieces, same minerals
        ■ Frost wedging – water freezes in cracks, expands about 9%
        ■ Abrasion – rocks scraped by wind, water, ice
        ■ Root wedging – plant roots grow into cracks
    ○ Chemical: minerals change into new substances
        ■ Oxidation – iron + oxygen → rust (red rocks)
        ■ Carbonation – acid rain dissolves limestone → caves
● Factors that affect weathering rate
    ○ Climate: warm + wet = fastest chemical weathering
    ○ Rock type: limestone weathers faster than granite
    ○ Surface area: more cracks = faster
● Erosion = moving sediment from one place to another
    ○ Agents: water (#1), wind, glaciers, gravity (mass movement)
    ○ Gravity examples: landslides, mudflows, creep, slump
● Deposition = sediment is dropped when the agent slows down
    ○ Delta – river enters ocean/lake
    ○ Sand dune – wind
    ○ Moraine – glacier
● Vocab to know: sediment, soil horizon, humus, meander, oxbow lake, terminal moraine
● Practice: be able to explain how a V-shaped valley (river) is different from a U-shaped valley (glacier)`,
