    name: "Fifth-grade book report on The Wild Robot",
    expect: "prose",
    text: `Book Report: The Wild Robot by Peter Brown
Ava Lindstrom
Grade 5, Room 12

The Wild Robot by Peter Brown is a science fiction novel about a robot named Roz who has to learn how to survive in the wilderness. It was published in 2016, and it is the first book in a series.

The story begins when a cargo ship sinks in a hurricane and crates full of robots wash up on a remote island. Only one robot survives. When some curious otters accidentally switch her on, Roz wakes up with no idea where she is or what she is supposed to do. At first the animals on the island think she is a monster and are scared of her. Roz learns by watching them and slowly figures out how to find shelter, avoid danger and even speak the animals' languages.

One day Roz accidentally destroys a goose nest. Only one egg survives, and Roz decides to take care of it. The gosling that hatches is named Brightbill, and Roz becomes his mother. Taking care of Brightbill helps Roz make friends with the other animals, and when a terrible winter comes, she builds a lodge where they can all stay warm. Later, other robots called RECOs come to the island to take Roz back, and the animals have to work together to protect her.

My favorite character is Brightbill because he is brave and funny, and he always sticks up for Roz even though she is different. My favorite part was when Brightbill learned to fly and left with the other geese for the winter, because it was sad but also happy.

I would recommend this book to anyone who likes animals, robots or adventure stories. It has a lot of short chapters and pictures, so it is easy to read, but it also makes you think about what it means to be part of a family. I would give it 5 out of 5 stars.`,
